      "color": "#b982a7",
      "description": "Zone 3 (centrilobular) hepatocytes: last to receive blood and poorest in oxygen, but richest in cytochrome P450 (CYP2E1). Site of glycolysis, lipogenesis and drug metabolism, so first to die in ischaemia, right heart failure ('nutmeg liver') and paracetamol overdose, and where alcoholic steatosis and hepatitis begin.",
